# privacy codec tests are durable (masking validation Layers 1-2) — re-include
!shared/privacy/tests/
# shared/library suites are durable: chunk_tables pins a SECURITY boundary (the
# table-HTML allowlist re-serializer feeding dangerouslySetInnerHTML) plus the
# "no raw TBL_ token ever reaches a reader" invariant, and reg_status pins the
# repeal vocabulary the reranker and aggregator read. Losing them loses the
# contract, and a clean clone would ship the sanitizer with nothing guarding it.
!shared/library/tests/
# masking backend-wiring tests are durable too (rest of backend/tests stays local-only)
!backend/tests/
backend/tests/*
!backend/tests/test_masking_wiring.py
# the aggregator prompt-identity suite is durable: adding the editorial variants
# meant extracting the three mode bodies out of PROMPT_MODE_*, and that refactor
# is only safe because those three prompts stayed byte-identical — asserted by
# pinned SHA-256 digests. Untracked, the guard protects one working tree and
# nothing else, and a later edit to a shared block would ship a silently changed
# in-app search prompt with nothing to catch it.
!agents/deep_search_v4/aggregator/tests/
agents/deep_search_v4/aggregator/tests/*
!agents/deep_search_v4/aggregator/tests/test_prompts_mode_body_identity.py
!agents/deep_search_v4/aggregator/tests/test_postvalidator_editorial.py
# access-tiers / library-gating suites are durable — they pin revenue and
# entitlement invariants (unlock idempotency, the frozen-library predicate, the
# شرح exclusion, the ISR cache-leak guard). Losing them loses the contract.
!backend/tests/test_library_gating.py
!backend/tests/test_library_enforcement.py
!backend/tests/test_library_mine.py
!backend/tests/test_rate_limit_library.py
!backend/tests/test_reference_source.py
!backend/tests/test_blog_snapshot_gating.py
# the public-blog sitemap + slug-keyed reveal suite is durable for the same
# reasons, on a wing whose failures are all silent: a feed that keeps listing a
# RETRACTED article resubmits it to Google forever, a listed subject with an
# empty urlset is the file `courts` was pulled for, and the reveal's 402 (never
# 401) is the one thing keeping an anonymous reader from being bounced off a
# public page into a login. None of the three shows up in a type or a 500.
!backend/tests/test_blog_sitemap_subjects.py
# the editorial publishing suite is durable — every invariant it pins is
# INVISIBLE at runtime. `support: bool = False` instead of Optional[bool]
# compiles, returns 200, and silently drops the support executor from every
# partially-pinned job; a headless ask_user pause looks like a live job for an
# hour and then fails; `editorial=True` never reaching build_retrieval_config
# publishes chat-voice answers as articles with nothing in any response to say
# so; and a v1 row whose blog_id != root_id breaks /seo, /cards and /retract at
# once. None of the four shows up in a type, a log line or a status code.
!backend/tests/test_editorial_publishing.py
# the public_blogs service suite is durable for the same wing and was SHIPPED
# WITHOUT ITS GUARD (commit d912137 carried the code, not this file). It pins the
# versioned write: that `append_version` goes through the migration-155 RPC —
# asserted as exactly one rpc call and ZERO manual updates on public_blogs, so
# reintroducing hand-rolled flipping fails here rather than in production — plus
# mint-time slug refusal, the reserved `subjects` literal, and H1 extract/strip.
# Its FakeDB also enforces the three unique indexes and rolls back refused
# writes; without that, any row-count assertion after a constraint violation is
# measuring debris.
!backend/tests/test_public_blogs.py
# المشتركون الأوائل — the early-adopter promo suite is durable for the same
# reason: it pins that a seat holder is precisely someone charged the promo
# price, that cancelling forfeits it and a refund does not, and that a renewal
# never discounts a non-member. All four are money, and none is visible in a
# type. Mutation-tested (17/17) — losing the file loses the proof.
!backend/tests/test_early_adopters.py
# what counts as a PURCHASE — the rule the post-payment intro tour fires on.
# Durable because it is invisible in every type: `plan_id != "free"` compiles
# fine and is wrong (dev grants, comps and expired terms all read as paid),
# which is exactly the bug this suite was written against.
!backend/tests/test_intro_tour_gate.py
# reference-card library links are durable — they pin that «فتح ... في ريحان» is
# NAVIGATION: never metered, never a guessed URL, and never present for a
# compliance service (that wing was retired, so any link there is a 404). They
# also pin the batching bound, which is what keeps a 20-reference panel from
# turning into 20 sidecar round-trips.
!backend/tests/test_reference_library_links.py
# payments is real money — the suite pins the arithmetic (halalas ×100, the
# inclusive VAT split, the prorated upgrade credit, the 2 SAR refund fee), the
# paid-path ORDER (snapshot before grant, refunded before revoke), the
# never-5xx webhook contract, and the boot guard that stops a live key charging
# real cards from a dev box.
!backend/tests/test_payments.py
# receipts guard the NO-TAX-LANGUAGE rule (no VAT registration) — durable.
!backend/tests/test_receipts.py
# edge-hardening suites are durable — they pin the deploy gate (origin lock must
# never 403 /api/v1/health, or every Railway deploy fails), the CORS-ordering
# invariant that once took production logins down, and the rate-limit bucket
# identity under forged CF-Connecting-IP / X-Forwarded-For headers.
!backend/tests/test_origin_lock.py
!backend/tests/test_client_ip_resolution.py
# navigation-hardening suites are durable — anon must NEVER be metered per-user
# (an IP key here would meter the ISR renderer and take the public library down),
# the 429 must stay a single shared contract, and the filter vocabularies pin the
# enumeration fix incl. the total_pages oracle.
!backend/tests/test_library_item_budget.py
!backend/tests/test_library_filter_hardening.py
# /search charges the SAME item budget as a hub page, on the same section:slug
# keys — that is what stops search being a way to buy extra corpus reach. It also
# carries the only coverage of the search half of the free/paid ladder. It was
# authored and then silently dropped by this very ignore rule; re-included.
!backend/tests/test_bm25_search.py
# sector-wing suites are durable for the same reason — they pin the §5 amendment
# to that enumeration fix (library_sectors.md D8): a VALIDATED sector is a
# SECTION, so it gets real counts, while a sector PLUS a free-text filter is
# filtered again and keeps the flat ceiling. Both spellings (Latin sector_slug /
# raw Arabic sector|domain) must behave identically or a caller just switches
# spelling. test_library_sectors.py is the drift guard the slug map's own
# docstring delegates to ("CI catches it") — which only holds if it is committed.
!backend/tests/test_library_sectors.py
!backend/tests/test_library_sector_wing.py
# court-section suite is durable for exactly the same reason, one axis over:
# «الجهة القضائية» is a SECTION too, so `court` must stay OUT of the `filtered`
# flag or `_visible_total_pages` pins every court page to 2 pages for anon —
# silently, over a 20,335-judgment section. It also pins that the 12-slug
# vocabulary resolves in memory (a reserved/unknown slug must never reach the
# DB) and that the raw `cases.court` variant tuples are matched EXACTLY, which
# is what keeps the counts stable enough to stay out of the oracle clamp.
!backend/tests/test_library_courts.py
# judgments-hub suite is durable — it pins the ranked-view contract that makes
# publishing past SAMPLE_MODE_MAX_IDS safe (no short pages, exact total_pages,
# slug carried by the relation) and the NULLS-LAST ordering. The ديوان/زكاة/تأمين
# feeds have no date_gregorian at all, so a NULLS-FIRST regression would bury
# every dated judgment behind ~11k dateless ones. It was local-only until
# 2026-08-08, which is why the ranked-view rewire broke 8 of its tests with CI green.
!backend/tests/test_library_judgments.py
# related-items suite is durable — it pins the two invariants the «اقرأ تاليًا» /
# «الأنظمة المذكورة» strips rest on, both of which fail SILENTLY rather than loudly.
# (1) The publish filter: related_items stores edges over the FULL corpus and the
# slug check happens at read time, so a regression that drops it renders dead links
# to unpublished أنظمة on every library page at once. (2) Fail-soft on a missing
# table: the backend must ship before or after migration 143 without 500ing, so
# there is a test that asserts a doc page survives `related_items` not existing.
# Neither shows up in a smoke test — the page still renders in both failure modes.
!backend/tests/test_library_related_items.py
# entity-sections suite is durable — it pins the two NON-EDITS that ARE the
# /compliance entity axis (compliance_entity_sections.md §2/D1), both of which
# fail SILENTLY. (1) `entity` stays out of `section_scoped`, which is what lets
# anon and free read an entity page at all — while the SECTOR axis on the same
# handler stays paid-only, and the suite asserts both halves, because
# "harmonising" them is the obvious wrong fix. (2) `entity` stays out of
# `filtered`, or the enumeration clamp pins anon total_pages to 2 and prints
# «1 2» over وزارة العدل's 115 guides with page 1 still rendering perfectly. It
# also carries the LIVE drift check against `services.provider_name`: the
# predicate is `eq`, so one retyped character is an empty section and a «0» tile
# — the plan's own §3 table had already lost a fatha, caught only by this file.
!backend/tests/test_library_entities.py
# case-provenance suite is durable — it pins the GATE SPLIT that D-CROSSWALK rests on:
# «المجلد»/«الصفحات» may render on an anonymous /judgments page, the مجلد PDF and
# collection URLs may not. One bound-volume PDF is ~50 full gated rulings, so a URL that
# drifts into the citation half publishes far more than the per-item MoJ link the original
# decision was written about — and it would do so silently, since both halves are
# list[dict[str, str]] and no type tells them apart. Also pins the volume registry's two
# key shapes (path vs sha1) against the int `source_volume` that looks like a key and is not.
!backend/tests/test_case_sources.py
# judgment publish-selector suite is durable — it pins the per-feed allocation
# (insurance takes ALL, shortfall redistributes), the sqrt court spread, and that
# the sector cap is scoped to the وزارة العدل slice. Sectors exist on NO other
# feed, so a globally-scoped cap silently stops constraining the one feed that
# has them. Also pins that no retired publish ceiling is live in the script.
!backend/tests/test_build_judgment_slugs.py
# account-settings suite is durable — it pins that /logout revokes via the
# SERVICE-ROLE admin API. Depending on the shared anon client there lets one
# user's logout globally revoke a DIFFERENT user's sessions, silently.
!backend/tests/test_account_settings.py
# preferred-name suite is durable — the value reaches the ROUTER's system
# instructions, so it pins the API-boundary cleaning (control chars and
# newlines stripped, 60-char cap) that keeps a display name from opening a
# fake instruction block. It also pins the compound-first-name rule: taking
# token[0] blindly addresses «عبد الله» as «عبد».
!backend/tests/test_preferred_name.py
# attachment-retention suite is durable — it pins that the daily sweep purges the
# FILE and never the row. message_attachments cascades off workspace_items, so a
# DELETE there silently destroys the OCR text (the only form of a document any
# agent ever reads), the WI-{seq} alias and the history tag in one statement.
# That is not hypothetical: it had already eaten 22 of 46 extractions before it
# was caught. Also pins UPDATE-before-DELETE, which is what makes a deploy
# landing ahead of migration 125 a no-op instead of unrecoverable file loss.
!backend/tests/test_attachment_retention.py
# «عرض المصدر» on the public_blogs wing. Durable because it pins an invariant
# neither surface can check alone: has_source=True is a PROMISE the reveal
# endpoint must keep — a True it then refuses sells the reader an unlock we
# cannot deliver, and for a chargeable family it sells it after taking payment.
# Also pins that the flag is NOT an entitlement signal (anon sees the button and
# gets a 402, never a 401) and that the legacy blog_posts stripper is unchanged.
!backend/tests/test_blog_reference_reveal_flag.py
# public_blogs.generation_context + review_status (migrations 157/158). Durable
# because every invariant it pins is invisible at runtime: the column is written
# by a background job, read by nobody and rendered nowhere, so a publish that
# stops writing it, writes a half-filled object, or leaks it into a public
# payload returns the same 200 with the same article. It pins the honest NULL
# (the forensic rows are best-effort, so "missing" is normal and a shell that
# reads as complete is worse), that a capture failure never fails a publish
# holding a finished article, the size guard's ORDER (bodies before structure —
# the live objects are 263 kB and 330 kB raw against a 9 kB article), and
# absence from every public response model asserted against the JSON schema.
!backend/tests/test_blog_generation_context.py
