.claude/deploy-*.png
# Ad-hoc capture artifacts that land at the REPO ROOT (and one level into
# agents/) whenever a Playwright/verification pass runs without an -o path:
# feature screenshots, scraped-response dumps, console-error transcripts.
# Root-anchored on purpose — real project images live under frontend/public,
# frontend/app and marketing/, and a blanket `*.png` would swallow all of them.
/*.png
/*.txt
agents/*.png
# Next dev-server stdout capture (the `*_dev.log` rule above misses this name)
frontend/dev.log

# graphify knowledge graph output
graphify-out/

# simple_search eval RUN ARTIFACTS — every one of these is written by a script
# in the same directory (results dumps, and the setup/teardown state files
# ab_setup.json / rerun_setup.json). The harness (*.py) is the durable part and
# stays tracked; re-running it regenerates all of this. Committed once by
# mistake in 0ff6f6f — ~1MB of dumps — and removed in the follow-up.
agents/simple_search/eval/*.json
agents/simple_search/eval/*.log

# Supabase CLI scratch state. `supabase/.temp/cli-latest` is a version-check
# marker the CLI writes on every invocation — machine-local, zero bytes of
# project content, and it reappears the moment anyone runs the CLI again.
supabase/.temp/
